The app will read in the fcm_make_ocean Rose configuration file (app/fcm_make_ocean/rose-app.conf)
and look for the following entries under [env]:

    * nemo_sources
    * nemo_project_location
    * nemo_base
    * nemo_rev

Git URLs will be cloned to local directories under ${ROOT_LOCAL} if these clones do not exist.
These local paths will be copied into another configuration file (app/fcm_make_ocean/opt/rose-app-gitpaths.conf),
which will be used by fcm_make_ocean as an optional configuration. The git URLs in app/fcm_make_ocean/rose-app.conf
will therefore be replaced by paths to local clones at fcm_make_ocean runtime.

Git URLs are any of:

    * <GIT>
    * <GIT>/<branch>
    * <GIT>@<hash>
    * <GIT>/<branch>@<hash>

where <GIT> is any repository URL matching one of:

    * (git@).*(.git)
    * (http://).*(.git)
    * (https://).*(.git)

<branch> is any git branch or tag name. <hash> is a git commit hash that should be valid for <branch>, which
can be given in truncated form (e.g. "abcd12" instead of "abcd1234567890abcde") as long as there is no ambiguity
with other commit hashes on the repository.

For the NEMO Gitlab, valid git URLs might be:

    * git@forge.nemo-ocean.eu:nemo/nemo.git                 # Current head, "main" branch
    * https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git             # "    "
    * https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git/test        # Current head, "test" branch
    * https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git/4.2.0       # Commit corresponding to the "4.2.0" tag, "main" branch
    * https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git@38d685      # Commit 38d6856256fa965ad93fdf3ee241d2dd2431575f, "main" branch
    * https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git/main@38d685 # "    "


The path conversions behave as follows, with <GIT> corresponding to "https://forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo.git":

    nemo_project_location
    =====================

        <GIT>             => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo
        <any_other_entry> => <NO CHANGE>

    nemo_base
    =========

        If nemo_project_location is a git path:

            <no_entry>        => main
            <any_other_entry> => <NO CHANGE>

        Otherwise, nemo_base is unchanged.

    nemo_rev
    ========

        If nemo_project_location is a git path:

            <any_octal_hash>  => /<SHORT_OCTAL>
            <any_other_entry> => /<HEAD>

            * <SHORT_OCTAL> is the first 6 characters of <any_octal_hash>
            * <HEAD> is the first 6 characters of the head commit of the git path.

        Otherwise, nemo_rev is unchanged.

    nemo_sources
    ============

        Each path in the list will be processed and replaced individually if needed.

        Absolute paths:

            <GIT>                           => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/main/<HEAD>
            <GIT>/branch                    => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/branch/<HEAD>
            <GIT>@abcd1234                  => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/main/abcd12
            <GIT>/branch@abcd1234           => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/branch/abcd12
            <SVN>:repos/absolute/path       => <NO CHANGE>
            <SVN>:repos/absolute/path@12345 => <NO CHANGE>
            /absolute/path                  => <NO CHANGE>

            * <SVN> is either "fcm" or "svn"
            * <HEAD> is the first 6 characters of the head commit of the git path

        Relative paths:

            If nemo_project_location is a git path (assumed here to be <GIT>):

                path          => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/path/<HEAD>
                path@abcd1234 => ${ROOT_LOCAL}/forge.nemo-ocean.eu/nemo/nemo/path/abcd12
                longer/path   => <NO CHANGE>

                * <HEAD> is the first 6 characters of the head commit of the git path

            Otherwise, the relative path is unchanged.
